
# v4256 -- NATIVE box3d build artifacts, for tools/ship/box3dFilter-selfcheck.mjs.
# Deliberately NOT committed, unlike vendor/box3d/box3d.wasm. The .wasm is
# architecture-independent and the ENGINE needs it at runtime; these are an
# x86_64 Linux .a and .o that only a gate uses, and shipping them would put a
# binary in the tree that is wrong on every other machine. Produce them with
# physics/box3d/build-box3d-native.sh; without them the gate skips that section
# and says so.
vendor/box3d/native/

# v4482 -- the terrain crate built for wasm32 by cargo alone, so tools/ship/erosionMeasure-selfcheck.mjs
# can time it. Same rule as vendor/box3d/native/ above: a build product of one box, never committed;
# the engine ships without it and world/terrainWasm.js says so.
wasm-terrain/target/
wasm-terrain/Cargo.lock
